# A2ML Profile: a2ml/state

@abstract:
Validation profile for the 6a2 STATE.a2ml metadata record (current project
state and progress). Non-executable: this profile only raises validation
strictness. It constrains exactly the five axes permitted by SPEC.adoc
Section 8.2.
@end

@profile-def(id=a2ml/state, version="1.0.0"):
required_sections:
  - metadata
  - position
  - maintenance-status
allowed_directives: closed [ profile ]
required_directives: []
reference_classes: []
min_attestation: checked
@end

# Notes

@rationale:
STATE documents are record-dialect A2ML (TOML-like [section] headers map to
A2ML section titles). The three required sections are the load-bearing ones:
`metadata` (identity/version), `position` (phase/maturity), and
`maintenance-status` (last-run result). `allowed_directives: closed [ profile ]`
keeps STATE a pure data record — the only directive permitted is the
`@profile` declaration itself; any stray markup directive is a checked-mode
error.
@end
